termbox2.h is an unmodified copy of upstream termbox2 (MIT licensed):

  https://github.com/termbox/termbox2
  commit cdf62e9990d8b200768780080fb10a4e2f680051 (2026-09-03, version 2.7.0-dev)
  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/termbox/termbox2/cdf62e9990d8b200768780080fb10a4e2f680051/termbox2.h

The compile-time options Term::Fabulous builds it with live in tf_termbox.h;
termbox2.c is the one translation unit that defines TB_IMPL.

Updating termbox2: the Term::Fabulous input parser in termbox2.c (Alt
keys, SGR mouse reports) hooks in through tb_set_func(TB_FUNC_EXTRACT_PRE)
and reads the input buffer global.in directly. Upstream marks tb_set_func
and TB_FUNC_EXTRACT_PRE for removal in version 3.x (ABI version 3, see the
"Deprecation notice" in termbox2.h). Before taking a 3.x release,
port tf_install_input_parser() to its replacement, then run t/termbox.t:
it feeds raw escape sequences through the parser.

Inline mode (tf_init_inline_rwfd() in termbox2.c) repeats the steps of
tb_init_rwfd() with termbox2's static init functions and empties the
TB_CAP_ENTER_CA, TB_CAP_EXIT_CA and TB_CAP_CLEAR_SCREEN entries of
global.caps; tf_cursor_position() appends to global.in, and
tf_reset_attrs() resets global.last_fg and global.last_bg. After
updating termbox2.h, compare tb_init_rwfd() with tf_init_inline_rwfd()
and check that tb_deinit() and resize_cellbufs() still take the screen
only through those capabilities; the "inline mode" subtest of
t/termbox.t checks the output.
